※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4524

※ A result whose type says its error carries a value has one in every failure
※ of it: there is no failure of such a type that carries nothing, so a `⊥`
※ written without a value would be making a value with a hole in it.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8?u16 = ⊥
    0u6
